<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  @bacons/apple-targets writes a default Info.plist into this folder ONLY when one does not
	  already exist (build/with-widget.js: `if (!fs.existsSync(filePath))`), and its README states
	  "The root Info.plist file in each target directory is not managed and can be freely
	  modified". So this file is committed (see mobile/.gitignore's `!targets/widget/Info.plist`
	  un-ignore) and prebuild leaves it alone.

	  The NSExtension dict below is byte-for-byte what the plugin generates for `type: "widget"`
	  (target.js `getTargetInfoPlistForType` default branch → NSExtensionPointIdentifier =
	  com.apple.widgetkit-extension). If the plugin is upgraded and starts emitting more keys for
	  widgets, they must be mirrored here by hand — that is the cost of owning this file.

	  UIAppFonts is why we own it. A widget extension is a separate bundle and cannot see the
	  fonts expo-font registers in the MAIN app's UIAppFonts, so Geist/Geist Mono have to be both
	  copied into this target (the .ttf files beside this plist, picked up automatically by the
	  target's PBXFileSystemSynchronizedRootGroup) and declared here. Names are relative to the
	  .appex resources root. Consumed by ForgeMachinedStyle.swift via Font.custom(PostScript name).
	-->
	<key>NSExtension</key>
	<dict>
		<key>NSExtensionPointIdentifier</key>
		<string>com.apple.widgetkit-extension</string>
	</dict>
	<key>UIAppFonts</key>
	<array>
		<string>Geist-Regular.ttf</string>
		<string>Geist-Medium.ttf</string>
		<string>Geist-SemiBold.ttf</string>
		<string>GeistMono-Regular.ttf</string>
		<string>GeistMono-Medium.ttf</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
